      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove those risks.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day, a common anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours:** 1,600\u20132,400 mg/day, for analgesia.\n\nDid you mean 1600 mg total per day, or one of the doses above? If you do intend 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
